                        </div>
                    

                    

                    



                    <div id="page-content">
                        

<div style="text-align: right;"><div class="page-rate-widget-box"><span class="rate-points">rating:&nbsp;<span class="number prw54353">-11</span></span><span class="rateup btn btn-default"><a title="I like it" href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.modules.PageRateWidgetModule.listeners.rate(event, 1)">+</a></span><span class="ratedown btn btn-default"><a title="I don't like it" href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.modules.PageRateWidgetModule.listeners.rate(event, -1)">&#8211;</a></span><span class="cancel btn btn-default"><a title="Cancel my vote" href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.modules.PageRateWidgetModule.listeners.cancelVote(event)">x</a></span></div></div>
<p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5187</p>
<p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Safe</p>
<p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5187 only requires the standard bullet-proof glass containment cell as they have no interest in leaving or harming others, however if necessary, the cell has vents that can spray nitrous oxide to knock SCP-5187 out.</p>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5187 can be described as a 6’4” female half elf, half centipede centaur with four centipede legs, a centipede pincer on its rear end, green eyes, and ginger hair, it speaks with a light Norse accent.</p>
<p>SCP-5187's legs can crush objects up to 56 kilograms, and its pincer can snap objects up to 39 kilograms. It can paralyze beings with a touch of its hand, turn invisible at will, and stretch its skin to devour its prey.</p>
<p>SCP-5187 can move at around 53 miles per hour, but cannot keep that speed for long. Despite the strength of SCP-5187's centipede limbs, they are not immune to 12-gauge shell bullets. SCP-5187 is also susceptible to fire, acid, and it is able to drown.</p>
<p>Despite SCP-5187's appearance, it is almost entirely immune to cold weather, but due to it being a mortal and half mammal, half insect creature, it does have a freezing point and can be killed if necessary.</p>
<div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav">
<div style="text-align: center;">
<p>&#171; <a class="newpage" href="/scp-xxxw">SCP-XXXW</a> | SCP-XXXX | <a class="newpage" href="/scp-xxxy">SCP-XXXY</a> &#187;</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="blockquote">
<p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5187 “Tikuni”</p>
<p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Researcher Karis</p>
<p><strong>Foreword:</strong> SCP-5187 described to the researcher that it has basic and advanced magical abilities used for defense as well as feeding on its prey (Swallowing its victim whole)</p>
<p><strong>&lt;Begin Log&gt;</strong></p>
<p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Hello SCP-5187, as you are aware, you have been captured by the SCP Foundation, you are here because you are an anomaly to this world’s view of what is considered to be normal. I am here to interview you, so please answer my questions.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5187:</strong> Alright, what would you like to know about me?</p>
<p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> First off, did you have a name before you were brought here and given the name SCP-5187?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5187:</strong> Yes, my name was Tikuni, it is pronounced Te-Coo-Nee.</p>
<p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Alright, how do you know so much English?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5187:</strong> I learned it while observing humans who entered the abandoned cabin that the SCP Foundation found me hiding in.</p>
<p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Next question, you mentioned you participate in ‘Feeding’, what does that entail?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5187:</strong> Well to put it bluntly, I use magic to make my flesh more malleable in order to swallow my prey whole as in order to be full, I have to eat a large mammal, which sometimes ends up being a human due to foolish people entering the cabin to hunt me down after hearing of my existence.<br />
Although most enter the cabin assuming that I’m a bear or something like that, so most end up running away and are likely sent to mental hospitals.<br />
Although one or two people stay to try to fight me, which just results in their death and my belly being filled.</p>
<p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Alright, well we won’t feed you humans here, but we can feed you whole pigs, is that alright with you?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5187:</strong> I only ate humans at times because they tried to harm me and were basically an easy target, so go ahead and feed me pigs, or whatever other large mammal is deemed appropriate for the Foundation to feed me.</p>
<p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Good, well feeding times are at 9 AM, 1 PM, and 7 PM daily, so keep that in mind. Next question, what abilities do you possess and what are your weaknesses?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5187:</strong> Well as I stated earlier, I can make my flesh malleable. I can also turn invisible, and paralyze individuals with a simple touch. I am highly resistant to cold weather, but I can be frozen at around -83 Fahrenheit, I can be damaged with 12-gauge shell bullets, I can be hurt with fire and acid, and I can also drown.<br />
My centipede legs can smash anything that is 56 kilograms or below, and my pincer is able to smash and lift anything that is 39 kilograms or below.</p>
<p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Alright, last two questions and the interview will be over. Do you require liquids to survive? And do you have any genitalia and reproductive organs?</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5187:</strong> Well, that second question is a bit crass, but I’ll answer both. Yes, I need water to survive, and yes, I have both a vaginal, and an anal canal, my vaginal canal is near the front of my centipede underbelly, and my anal canal is near the back of my centipede underbelly, and yes, I have reproductive organs.</p>
<p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Well, that concludes this interview, thank you for being honest with me.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-5187:</strong> Goodbye researcher, and no problem.</p>
<p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> Researcher Karis has expressed that the interview went well. SCP-5187 does not remain a threat to the Foundation to this day, but most researchers remain cautious of SCP-5187.</p>
</div>

